  "observations": [
    "The public curve_fit module shrank from 583 to 257 lines. The adaptive implementation and existing banded-versus-dense solver comparison moved into a private module. The extracted implementation body is byte-identical after removing its visibility qualifier.",
    "The quarter arc at 0.001 has six controls in the joined full fit. Each independently trimmed half has four controls. Its first handle differs by more than 1e-8 from the joined fit. Matching separate halves is insufficient to establish the joined construction.",
    "Native quarter-half outputs agree exactly across the captured unit and source domains. The remaining records retain polynomial source, domain and reversal behavior without extrapolating a global joining rule.",
    "Fourteen previously supported Loft records and nine closest-point queries match complete native records. Twenty-two full or trimmed cases still require subdivision and fail explicitly. No sampled substitute or alternate fitter was added.",
    "Existing straight, polygon, initial-smooth and corrected-smooth regressions pass in both backends. Source-to-fit certificates and resource ceilings remain unchanged. Full scalar SDK parity and general smooth Loft Refit remain unfinished."
  ],
